# WP21 p9 (Far): a prefab instance (WP21_Span: 4 cubes 1500 cm apart) is expanded when the world is cooked, so its
# records land in 4 cells, each placed by its own bounds. Build HLODs cuts the same expanded world
# (ExpandWorldForCook), so the cook finds every saved HLOD fresh.
# Editor step here (the scenario player drives only the editor): Build HLODs on WP21_PrefabSpan_Far.
# Then, outside the editor (CLI, the proof of the cook and the runtime):
#   WorldCook Content/Scenes/WP21_PrefabSpan_Far.desce --project Projects/Desert/Desert.deproj --no-registry --verify
#     --out <CookedWorldDirectory>  -> code 0, "records back from the cells, equal to the expanded source (1 prefab instances)"
#   Runtime --project Projects/Desert/Desert.deproj --scene Content/Scenes/WP21_PrefabSpan_Far.desce --shot-frames …
#     near: 4 cubes drawn as meshes, 4 cells loaded; far: 4 HLOD stand-ins, no holes, 0 cells loaded.
Проект Projects/Desert/Desert.deproj --scene Content/Scenes/WP21_PrefabSpan_Far.desce
Дано run Panel "Open World Partition"
Когда run Scene "Build HLODs"
Тогда wp21_far_built HLODs построены без ошибки (в журнале «[Build HLODs] 'WP21_PrefabSpan_Far': 4 cell(s) … 0 stale»); вид сцены с префабом
